---
title: Rule structure - Strategy, Composite, and a Factory
---
classDiagram
    direction TB
    class RuleFactory {
        <<factory>>
        +rulesFor(org) Rule
    }
    class Rule {
        <<interface>>
        +check(ctx) Violation[]
    }
    class RuleEngine {
        -root Rule
        +validate(ctx)
    }
    class CompositeRule {
        -children Rule[]
        +add(r Rule)
        +check(ctx)
    }
    class RestRule
    RestRule : +check(ctx)
    class QualificationRule
    QualificationRule : +check(ctx)

    RuleFactory ..> Rule : creates
    RuleEngine --> "1" Rule : holds one

    %% the diamond goes on the whole (CompositeRule).
    %% the old PNG had it on the Rule end, which is backwards
    CompositeRule o-- "*" Rule : children

    Rule <|.. CompositeRule
    Rule <|.. RestRule
    Rule <|.. QualificationRule

    note for RuleEngine "The engine holds one Rule. In practice that Rule<br>is a CompositeRule holding the blocking rules,<br>which holds another CompositeRule for the warnings.<br>Nothing above the engine knows the difference."
